-- Arena challenges batch 5/14: rows 101-125 (track: Digital Electronics, category: ECE)

Method: Sum of powers of 2 for each ''1'' bit.','{"choices": ["9", "11", "13", "7"], "correct": 1}'::jsonb,'1×2³ + 0×2² + 1×2¹ + 1×2⁰ = 8 + 0 + 2 + 1 = 11. Binary is base-2; each bit represents a power of 2.','{multiple_choice}'::text[],0.9) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

XOR: output is 1 when odd number of inputs are 1.','{"choices": ["0", "1", "Depends on gate type", "Always 0 with 3 inputs"], "correct": 0}'::jsonb,'3-input XOR: 1 XOR 1 XOR 0 = 0 XOR 0 = 0. XOR counts parity: even number of 1s → 0, odd number of 1s → 1. Here 2 ones (even) → output = 0.','{multiple_choice}'::text[],0.82) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

MUX selects I_(S₁S₀).','{"choices": ["0", "1", "Alternates between 0 and 1", "Undefined"], "correct": 1}'::jsonb,'S₁S₀ = 01 = 1 in decimal → select I₁ = 1. Output = 1. A 4-to-1 MUX with 2 select lines routes one of 4 inputs. MUXes can implement any Boolean function of 2 variables.','{multiple_choice}'::text[],0.8) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

Apply binary addition; discard carry out of MSB.','{"choices": ["31", "−31", "31 with overflow", "−70"], "correct": 0}'::jsonb,'0110 0101 + 1011 1010 = 1 0001 1111. Discard carry: 0001 1111 = 31. 101 + (−70) = 31. No overflow since operands have opposite signs — overflow only occurs when same-sign operands produce opposite-sign result.','{multiple_choice}'::text[],0.72) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;
